# `@Flatten` of a dynamic of dynamics that is not a `rebuild`'s (Semantics Appendix B:
# "`@Flatten` follows a `rebuild`'s dynamic, or any other `$$a` a program holds"; the
# Compiler book's seed, `@Flatten` driven by its outer's update event): the outer here is a
# hold of dynamics, as Type System ch. 4's `$$title`, whose inners are the page's holds
# taken whole by `$Sel`, so the outer fires only on the swap. The flattened value follows
# its inner in the inner's tick; when the outer fires at n the flatten adopts, after n, the
# inner the outer then holds, and from n+1 reads and fires with it (the tick owed). Written
# by Claude on the claude-lowering branch; subject to change.
emit Ui.*
test mod Tests

$Sel: fn Bool, $Nat, $Nat -> $Nat
fn $Sel useB, $p, $q = if useB: $q else: $p

@page: @unit
@page:
    !inc <- Ui.Button(label=$"inc")                         # 0
    !swap <- Ui.Button(label=$"swap")                       # 1
    $a <- 0 then $a + 1 on !inc
    $b <- 100 then $b + 1 on !inc
    $$cur <- $a then $Sel (True on !swap), $a, $b
    $shown <- @Flatten $$cur
    Ui.Label(text=$"{$shown}")                              # 2
